title: 'Stasser and Titus (1985), and Stasser, Stewart and Wittenbaum (1995): groups discuss what all members know far more than what one knows, and rarely find a choice visible only by pooling; knowing who is expert in what helps.'
pid: 95a8b86b-cb0e-4e56-8d47-49388fae9f69
body: |2-
  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hidden_profile
  Summary: Wikipedia and citing papers found by search; unchecked
  against the papers. Assigned expertise helps when goals are shared,
  and hurts when they compete. Took: a proposer leads with what only
  its territory shows; the team note and the maps say who knows what.
